Manual re-runs at synthesis (2026-10-16), for the two scripts the harness could not run as copied:
logic/checks/c0_rerun_scout.py: needs a scratch dir argument and the scout folder; run as
  python3 c0_rerun_scout.py <scratch>/c0scratch research/scouts/novel-logic/checks  -> exit 0; stdout byte-identical to the saved c0_rerun_scout.out
  (it re-runs scout N1's c1_lottery and c3_threshold: both byte-identical to the scout's saved outputs).
terms/checks/t6_revision.py: imports scout S's s2_craig_blowup from ../../../scouts/sfi/checks relative to itself; run in a
  scratch tree mirroring research/ (tracks/terms/checks and scouts/sfi/checks copied) -> exit 0, 11.9 s; t6_revision.out byte-identical.
Not re-run at synthesis (long; reproduced in the thread's revision round and by its referee): philosophy c4_mars_pool.py (4692 s in
  the thread), c4b_volume_crosscheck.py (did not finish in 72 min), c8_mars_distances.py (superseded for its table by c10),
  c10_distances_research.py (2131 s); c9_revision.py, which imports c4's model code, was re-run (rerun_checks_long.out).
pyerfa: the Kepler scripts need pyerfa 2.0.1.5 (as the threads used); it was installed into a scratch library folder outside the
  repository and put on PYTHONPATH for rerun_checks_pyerfa.out and rerun_checks_long.out.
